---

## 10. Scope and final disposition

The theorem uses only the already-audited orbit crossing-mass identities and the
current shared endpoint-retention theorem.  It adds no train-order geometry, KKT-weight
bound, response estimate, or source motion.

The improvement is small in `t` but exact in structure: the residual atomic mass can
pay its square contribution only once, so the dominant orbit is larger than the old
`MA` relaxation records.

The safe current proof-only full-core Type-II floor becomes

\[
\boxed{1.83287}.
\]

C-II remains open.  The natural next step is to use the per-phase-class constraints
inside the dominant orbit from the `g=0.0050` two-leaf minimax theorem, rather than
collapsing the entire dominant orbit to one total mass `M`.

**Final verdict:** PASS at proof-only full-core Type-II scope.
